{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4723",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is implicated in the interaction with Ndufv1 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which in turn participates in the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity, ultimately leading to Ndufv1 being a participant in this process. This indicates that Metformin may influence the activity of Nadh Dehydrogenase, potentially through a mechanism involving the subunit Ndufa12 or Ndufv3. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact mechanism by which Metformin affects Ndufv1 remains to be fully elucidated. The overlapping roles of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in the same pathway highlight the importance of these subunits in the metabolic process, reinforcing the hypothesis that Metformin modulates Nadh Dehydrogenase activity, which in turn may impact Ndufv1.",
